diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..4699f77 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,39 @@ After making changes to this gem, you need to update Fizzy to pick up the change
 BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 ```
 
+## Billing
+
+| Plan | Key | Price | Cards | Storage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free | `free_v1` | Free | 1,000 | 1 GB |
+| Unlimited | `monthly_v1` | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB |
+| Unlimited+ | `monthly_extra_storage_v1` | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB |
+
+Plans live in `Subscription`, one class per plan, named after the Queenbee short name
+of the plan. The Stripe price for a paid plan is read from `STRIPE_#{KEY}_PRICE_ID`.
+
+Stripe hosts both checkout and the customer portal. `Account::SubscriptionsController`
+and `Account::BillingPortalsController` send people over there and Stripe posts
+everything that happens back to `/stripe/webhooks`, where `Account::Subscription.process`
+mirrors it into `account_subscriptions`.
+
+An account with no active subscription is on the free plan. When it runs out of cards
+it can still draft, but publishing and creating over the API are refused, the create
+buttons give way to an upgrade, and the last hundred cards count down. Paid plans lift
+the card limit and bring their own storage allowance.
+
+### Support tools
+
+`/admin/accounts` lists the accounts and each one has a page with what it's on and what
+it's using:
+
+* **Comp** and **Uncomp** waive the bill entirely (`account_billing_waivers`). Comped
+  accounts are never charged and never held to a limit.
+* **Override** records what an account counts as using (`account_overridden_limits`),
+  for when what we measured is wrong — card numbers come from a counter that never goes
+  down, so an account that deleted half its cards still reads as full. **Reset** drops
+  the override and goes back to what we measured.
+
 ## Working with Stripe
 
